WEBVTT

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:02.980
What?

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.920
So Kanamecchi, your parents are leaving today...

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.480
to travel abroad for four days and three nights?

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.810
Yeah.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.420
They managed to get some time off,

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.010
so they're heading off with Hisako's parents.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.530
Sounds wonderful.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.330
I see.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.660
I guess that means you'll
 be home alone, Kaname.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.790
You won't be able to 
see your beloved mom.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.470
Hey, are you going to be okay...

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.430
being so far away from 
her for three whole days?

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.310
I'll be perfectly fine!

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.610
What sort of character are you trying...

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.720
to make me out to be, anyway?

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.940
If the Tsukahara mother and son 
can last three whole days apart,

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.610
we'd better submit it to the
 Guinness Book of World Records.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.090
I know, right?

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.330
But, will you really be okay?

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:45.390
What about dinner?

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.290
I'll be eating next door 
while my mom's gone.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.590
Hisako's sister said she'd 
make dinner for me.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.020
Shizuna-oneechan, you mean?

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:55.650
Yeah.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:00.080
I don't know if she's suddenly 
taken an interest in cooking,

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.950
but she's been practicing a lot.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.620
Going over there just to eat is 
such a pain in the ass.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.110
But I guess it's better than 
cooking for myself,

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.660
so I have no choice.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.080
I see.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.550
What a pain.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.930
But Kaname-kun, you look 
kinda happy about it.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.570
I cut too much off.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.280
No way, he's here already?

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.270
You're here early.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.360
Were you asleep?

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.840
Your hair's a mess.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.880
What?

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.510
Um, something like that.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:07.040
Where's Shizu-nee?

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:10.790
Oh, she's just getting ready.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.540
Welcome, Kaname-kun.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.240
Shizu-nee.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.180
I thought I was only here to eat.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.640
Of course not.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.850
If you don't work, you don't eat.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.140
You'll be helping me again tomorrow.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.940
And the day after, you'll do the shopping.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.730
I want you to go to the 
supermarket with Hisako-chan.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.330
What?

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.540
What?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.370
That's too much work.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.820
There's going to be a big sale on eggs tomorrow,

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.700
but they're limited to one carton per customer.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:46.490
That's why I want both of you to go.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.790
Shizu-nee, your sleeves will get wet.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.170
Huh? Oh.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.540
Jeez... Here.

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.240
It's okay. I can do it myself.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.540
Just let me.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.330
Delicious.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:14.270
The three of us haven't 
eaten together in a while.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.560
We used to go to each other's 
houses all the time.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.600
Kaname-kun, aren't you going to come over...

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.130
to show me your 100% test scores anymore?

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.500
No.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.350
That's right, sis.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:29.160
He can't get full marks now 
 that he's in high school.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.000
I wouldn't come even if I did!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.340
Mind if I have some more?

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.860
Go ahead.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:36.330
You must love my curry.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.230
No, I'm just so hungry, anything tastes good.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:42.670
You're always so mean.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.630
My sister's expanding her 
repertoire like crazy right now.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.080
What's she going to do when it's bigger?

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.650
Meet prospective suitors?

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:53.590
I guess no one would marry 
you if you couldn't cook.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:54.790
Sounds like a good idea.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.500
You should learn to make 
meat and potatoes next...

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:01.900
What?

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.610
Kaname-kun, your mother didn't tell you?

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.820
Tell me what?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.240
I'm getting married.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.750
To a co-worker of mine.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.860
Oh? That's odd.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.420
I went over to tell your mother 
just the other day.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.460
Kaname-kun?

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:23.670
Huh?

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:24.720
Oh, yeah.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.810
That's great. Congratulations.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:29.220
Thanks.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.720
You're getting married, huh? 
I had no idea.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:34.830
I see.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.360
Is he reading?

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.120
No, he can't be.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.900
He hasn't turned the page in ages.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:49.480
Kaname-kun has seemed down all morning.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.660
I wonder what's wrong...

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:54.770
Maybe Captain Comeback's 
cutting back on his hours?

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.120
We <i>are</i> in a recession.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.290
That's not it, kids.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:02.880
This is a case of a rabbit 
dying from loneliness.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.540
Huh? Why is he lonely?

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:06.890
You don't think...

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:09.550
That's right! He's trying to be strong,

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.650
but he's taking it hard...

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:13.600
Not seeing his mom!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.000
Can't you see it?

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.410
Can't you see his eyes, red with tears...

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.900
like a little bunny's every night?

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:24.640
The only time I've seen Kaname's eyes 
red is when they're red with rage.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:27.950
I wonder if there's anything we can do.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:31.790
I know. I'll bring back Kaname's mom.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:32.970
It'll take four days and three nights.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.410
You just want to travel abroad.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.080
I've got a good idea.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.380
Kaname-kun's late.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.530
He was already here by this time yesterday.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:46.300
Yeah.

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:50.320
Maybe Kaname's not planning 
on coming over to eat today.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.680
You're late. Dinner's already...

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.560
Good evening!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.270
My, my. What are you all doing here?

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.990
It's good to see you again!

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:08.120
Because Kanamecchi's broken-hearted 
about not seeing his mother,

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.240
we've come over today to cheer 
him up with a fun dinner party!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.560
That sounds like fun. Come on in.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.120
All right! Excuse the intrusion.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.790
My mother made this stew, if you'd like it.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.670
This is our sautéed and simmered burdock.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.620
This is yesterday's leftover 
meat and potatoes.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.760
Thank you.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.140
You're heartbroken because 
you can't see your mom?

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.110
Of course not.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:37.800
I told them I'm not, but they 
insisted on eating with us,

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.980
so I had to bring them over.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.310
You seem relieved.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:42.310
What?

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.280
Nothing.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.650
Sorry for bringing all 
these people, Shizu-nee.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.380
It's okay.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:53.970
They brought us food,

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:56.320
and it's always more fun 
to eat with lots of people.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.500
Really? That's good, then.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:05.440
Ouch. These onions hurt so much.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.860
You can do it.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.710
Imagine that ginger-fried pork 
right before your eyes.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.270
But I can't see!

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:12.340
I can't see it through my tears!

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:14.190
What is this?

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:17.300
This just seems like a last ditch 
attempt to avoid being eaten.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.440
You're the ones who said 
you'd cook for yourselves.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.020
Shut up and cut your onions.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.090
But we're not joking this time!

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:27.270
That's right.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.890
It's not just us; the entire nation 
would be in tears over this.

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.590
Switch with us! Kanamecchi, you cut next!

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:36.270
Kaname, you won't cry.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.460
Your heart isn't pure enough.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.820
Don't give me that.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.120
How rude.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.410
Ow!

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.880
No, no, I can't do this. 
I can't keep my eyes open.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:52.510
Then, just cut it with your eyes closed.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.400
I'll cut my hand off!

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.050
You don't have a choice.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.220
The word "shouga-yaki" originates
 from the phrase "shou ga nai."

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.220
<i>[Shouga-yaki - ginger-fried foods; 
shou ga nai - no choice, can't help it, etc.]</i>

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.720
It does not!

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:02.310
Oh?

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:03.930
Kaname-kun.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:09.790
Do you think we could use 
some of your soy sauce?

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.660
We don't have much left.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:14.700
Yeah, sure. I'll go get some.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.990
Jeez, I can't believe that slave driver.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.870
Soy sauce, soy sauce...

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.080
I can't cut onions anymore!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.130
Miss, please switch with me!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.190
Okay, okay.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.550
Good try.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:40.640
I didn't ask how much 
soy sauce she needed.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.840
Maybe I should take the big one.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:48.450
Soy sauce, soy sauce...

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:50.870
<i>Your mother didn't tell you?</i>

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:52.360
Soy sauce, soy sauce...

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:58.100
<i>I'm getting married 
to a co-worker of mine.</i>

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.080
Married?

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:09.920
Why do you have to get married?

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.340
See you later.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.810
Thanks for having us.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.810
Thanks for the food.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.590
That was amazing.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:29.350
They were as loud as grade 
schoolers having lunch.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:32.560
Well, tomorrow, the three 
of us can have a nice, quiet—

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.400
Hisako.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.260
I'll pass on dinner tomorrow.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.220
What?

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.880
It's too much work to come over 
here and help with things.

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.330
Too much work?

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.080
Tell Shizu-nee for me.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.220
See you later.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.410
Wait, Kaname!

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.460
Has everyone left?

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:56.670
Yeah.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.730
I see.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:01.640
Don't forget to buy two cartons 
of eggs with Kaname tomorrow.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:05.670
Oh, about that. Kaname just said...

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:07.270
What should I make?

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.170
We'll have lots of eggs,

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:11.460
so I was thinking either 
omelet rice or oyakodon.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:17.990
You're not going to cut your bangs?

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:19.330
Huh?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.340
You've been keeping it long for a while.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:25.400
I look young if I cut my bangs.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:28.870
Young? You're only 25.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.000
I'm already 25.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:37.070
So, should we have omelet rice 
or oyakodon tomorrow?

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:43.090
I'll ask Kaname!

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.800
It's me. Do you have a minute?

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:55.900
What do you want?

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.570
Don't give me that.

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.180
Your door wasn't locked.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:00.860
Oh.

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:02.510
Oh?

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:03.420
Well?

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.120
I wanted to talk to you 
about dinner tomorrow.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.860
Are you sure you won't come eat?

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:09.940
I told you, I'll pass.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:12.410
But my sister asked us to 
buy two cartons of eggs...

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:16.090
at the supermarket because 
they're on sale tomorrow.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:20.480
She's going to make either 
omelet rice or oyakodon with them.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.780
We wouldn't have to 
help much with those.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:27.230
Which do you prefer, Kaname?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.060
Either's fine.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:33.810
I haven't had omelet rice recently.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.480
Why don't you make that, then?

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:39.590
Don't say that. Think about—

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:41.860
Like I said, either's—

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:44.400
Ow, that hurt!

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:45.360
What was that for?

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:48.220
Because you're answering 
like you don't even care!

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:50.190
If her marriage bothers you this much,

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:51.910
you should've told her how you feel already!

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:54.850
What? What are you—

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.350
It's obvious!

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:59.940
I've known that you
 like my sister for ages!

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.870
You should just tell her.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:05.720
Maybe nothing will come 
of it, but at least...

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.760
It's fine.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.370
It's fine.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:16.650
It's not like that, anyway.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:21.910
I never thought about 
telling her or dating her.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:26.520
It's more like I look up to her, so...

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.580
But...

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:33.700
Kaname, you love her.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.380
Even if you look up to 
her, you still love her.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:42.360
Hey, wait. Why are you crying?

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:43.730
Hold on.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:45.170
Here, have a tissue.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:49.930
Tell her, you idiot!

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.430
What's her problem?

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:56.930
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.470
<i>I have too much on my mind.</i>

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:07.440
<i>I don't feel like going to 
the supermarket to buy eggs.</i>

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:11.620
Kaname-kun, good timing.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.890
I was just on my way over.

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:16.050
I thought we could go to 
the supermarket together.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:21.710
Hisako-chan has a quiz tomorrow, 
so she doesn't have time to go.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:24.900
She told me to go instead.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.160
That meddler...

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.210
Kaname-kun?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.930
Is something wrong?

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.500
Oh, not at all.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.930
Let's go, then.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.940
<b>Hanamaru Supermarket</b>

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.440
Two cartons of eggs.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:48.390
Are you really going 
to use all those?

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:51.520
You can never have too many eggs.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.490
You can use them to make 
all sorts of dishes.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:57.660
Now that I've expanded my 
repertoire, just leave it to me.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.660
Oh, sorry.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:03.300
Not at all. Sorry.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.910
Why are you spacing out like that?

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.590
I was wondering what 
we were having for dinner.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.970
That's all you ever think about.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.500
Kaname-kun!

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.140
Kaname-kun, over here!

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:21.290
You don't need to shout. What?

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.150
Don't give me that.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.480
When I turned around, you were gone.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.470
Here, this is for you.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:28.240
Hey...

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.780
We can't just try that.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.590
What if we end up having to buy it?

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.540
You worry too much.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.700
It's only a sample, so don't 
get so worked up. Just eat it.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:44.250
I had already decided to buy it 
before I started to eat it.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.740
You're the one getting worked up.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.270
Would you like another one?

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:52.580
Yes, please.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.230
How much are you going to eat?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:57.200
You two are quite the couple.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:01.730
I would've bought some even 
if you hadn't said that.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.260
Why, thank you.

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:08.320
We bought so much.

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:11.650
Sorry. I always end up getting more...

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.570
when there's a guy to help me carry.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:15.730
If you knew it was gonna be heavy,

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:19.510
I wish you'd been faster deciding 
which taiyaki flavor you wanted.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:22.080
Sorry, sorry.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.080
Let's take a break.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.710
<b>Hanamaru Supermarket</b>

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:32.260
Hey, don't blame me if 
you spoil your dinner.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.220
It's okay.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:42.060
Here.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:55.110
Okay, I'm next!

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.370
Hakkeyoi, nokotta!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.370
I win!

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.120
Darn it!

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.080
<i>Shizu-nee, look!</i>

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:07.940
<i>I found some awesome grass!</i>

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.710
<i>No matter who I play 
grass sumo with, it never loses!</i>

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:14.310
<i>That's amazing, Kaname-kun.</i>

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:36.060
Hakkeyoi, nokotta!

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:39.380
I lost again.

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:41.800
Kaname-kun, you're so good at this.

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:44.210
Shizu-nee, you're just too weak.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:46.330
You should choose some stronger grass.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:49.460
I'm trying.

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:02.460
Um, about your... wedding.

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:03.270
What?

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.930
Uh, well...

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.160
What's he like? Is he good looking?

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:13.230
Oh, I don't know if I'd say that.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:17.360
All my friends say he kinda 
looks like Mori no Kuma-san.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.410
What? That's harsh.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:22.720
But he's nice.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:28.580
Not just to me, but to everyone.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.170
What about the ceremony?

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:33.460
When is it?

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:36.280
You'll have to find somewhere to live.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:40.710
Do you think, you know, 
you'll end up pretty far from here?

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.580
I guess you'll be okay with cooking.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.680
You've been expanding your 
repertoire recently.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:48.530
It's amazing.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:51.420
The most I can do is wash rice...

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.370
That's because you're so clumsy.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:03.200
Clumsy? I know I'm not 
good at cooking, but...

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:06.200
No, you're clumsy.

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:10.260
Not just at cooking, but everything.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.710
You're not better than anyone else.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:21.310
You study hard when no one's looking,

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:24.080
and even though you're clumsy,

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.680
if anyone asks you for help,

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:29.590
you always try to do more 
than you're capable of.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:34.230
But you never try to show that 
side of yourself to anyone.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:39.990
I know, because we've been 
together since you were little.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:44.860
Well, anyway, that's what's good about you.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:47.800
That you try so hard without expecting praise.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:49.060
I got praise.

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:52.220
You gave me praise, Shizu-nee.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.160
You'd call me amazing and smile.

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:59.430
I was really happy when 
you smiled for me.

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:06.360
<i>When I was little, I would do 
anything to get her attention.</i>

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:11.690
<i>100% test scores, 
back hip circles, report cards,</i>

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.360
<i>the first time I became Class President...</i>

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:19.040
<i>I showed her anything 
I could brag about.</i>

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:24.690
<i>She was always so close.</i>

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:30.010
<i>She always smiled for me.</i>

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.070
<i>I never thought about confessing to her.</i>

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.880
<i>I never thought about dating her.</i>

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:42.500
<i>But still, I...</i>

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:04.150
They're playing grass sumo.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:06.300
So weird.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:08.910
Playing kids' games 
even though they're adults.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:10.810
They're just big kids! Big kids!

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:15.160
We should get going.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:17.130
Kaname-kun, you can wash the rice.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.990
Sure.

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:20.530
Kaname-kun.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.150
Do you want omelet rice or oyakodon?

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:29.120
Oyakodon.

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:35.980
Did you tell her yesterday?

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:37.130
Tell her what?

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:41.620
Did you tell my sister you like her?

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:42.820
No.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:43.940
What?

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:47.520
But... what are you doing?

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:49.160
Why do you think I set that up?

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:51.610
I told you, it's fine.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:55.610
It's fine.

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:58.080
Thanks for everything.

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.880
Maybe I'll let my bangs grow out.

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:09.810
Who, you?

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:10.760
No way.

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:13.840
You'll totally give up and 
cut them before they've grown.

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:17.100
That's not true.

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:20.530
I'll definitely do it this time.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:23.860
Oh, right.

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:27.580
My sister made lunch for me today.

00:22:27.580 --> 00:22:29.890
Complete with a 
whole load of fried eggs.

00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:31.430
Seriously?

00:22:31.430 --> 00:22:33.370
She said she expanded her repertoire,

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:35.250
and all she's making is fried eggs?

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:42.690
Stripped Bare

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:20.110
Navel and Dignity

00:24:17.290 --> 00:24:19.480
The next episode is "Navel and Dignity."
